# Power regulator, on the configsettings page of the instr selector.
# A .ui entry is not run as a program: Nebulae itself handles it (ui.py,
# mode = the name after the number, here "power_regulator").
# Speed click on it: the speed encoder picks the value, shown in the colour of
# both speed LEDs: off = red, yield spin = green, shell spin = blue,
# nohlt = yellow. Speed click sets it and goes back to the instrument; pitch
# click goes back without a change. Keeps the CPU from sleeping (its
# wake-ups are heard as a tone): Code/scripts/quiet.sh spin. nohlt is a
# kernel option: choosing it (or leaving it) saves the settings and restarts
# the Pi.
# Slot LED bright = not off (nebulae-status).
